# Digests of the guest kernel, initramfs and busybox that nodo installs, pinned
# in-tree.
#
# install.sh names a release TAG (GUEST_KERNEL_VERSION), and a tag is mutable.
# Verifying a download against a SHA256SUMS fetched from that same release only
# proves the bytes arrived intact: whoever can edit the release swaps the artifact
# and its checksum together, and every new node boots a different guest kernel
# without a word. Verifying against these committed digests turns the tag into an
# immutable content reference, so bumping the kernel is a reviewable diff -- the
# same reason bash/guest-kernel/build.sh pins KERNEL_SHA256 for the upstream
# tarball instead of trusting cdn.kernel.org.
#
# When bumping GUEST_KERNEL_VERSION in install.sh, update TAG and all six digests
# here, and check them against the CI artifacts of the run that built them
# (`gh run download <run-id>`) and not only against the release assets -- the
# artifact store and the release are two independent copies of the same build.
#
# The initramfs is checkable a third way, which the kernel and busybox are not:
# it is byte-reproducible, so rebuilding it from this commit against the pinned
# busybox must reproduce the published digest exactly. Verified for arm64 across
# two unrelated machines -- an Ubuntu 24.04 CI runner and a Fedora Asahi M1 with
# 16 KiB pages -- so a digest that does not reproduce means the release, not the
# host that checked it.
#
#   gh release download guest-kernel --pattern busybox-linux-arm64 --dir /tmp/gk
#   bash bash/guest-kernel/build-initramfs.sh arm64 /tmp/gk /tmp/gk/busybox-linux-arm64
#
# A missing entry below is not a soft failure: download_guest_asset refuses to
# install an asset it has no pinned digest for. That is deliberate -- an
# unverifiable guest is worse than a failed install.
TAG guest-kernel
ada7f26f5d29ba3729f4c8741445ad0f0ebdebde82da6b8b295d2f25d9e10464  busybox-linux-amd64
a1be8bf6c15883c04ffeac0ca56188bc40fcc4198617758c444b7cbbda21dc23  busybox-linux-arm64
5dc019f2ec2bdaa8df4711b81f9b1e3662c5a8d0f738e5eabe596c52ddd72108  initramfs-linux-amd64
4ff0e0b6667186cbfbb86286bfdf4cd9287a9782cbc7d2f289a095b521006991  initramfs-linux-arm64
a8c7fa0a338daba08032f2bf9576eb59eb1389bcdf66882b9f4e1942b8623124  vmlinuz-linux-amd64
010c2237fc10dd40329e9539297a52f93948c39e918100bc901c4ef74b0d85da  vmlinuz-linux-arm64
